{
  "$comment": [
    "Proposed Brazilian Portuguese patterns for src/data/claims-lint.json (patterns['pt-BR'] of each rule) and src/data/keyword-map.json (seOwned['pt-BR'], seOwnedLead['pt-BR'], reserved.G1['pt-BR']). Not merged: the owner decides (M3 pt-BR translator, 2026-10-06; QA record pt-BR-qa.md §5).",
    "Coverage: every claims-lint rule with per-locale patterns and no pt-BR key yet (25 rules). Skipped: selection-translate and jargon (already have pt-BR), io-home and engine-claim ('*' only).",
    "Matching as in the validator: case-insensitive with the u flag, on the rendered text (placeholders filled, markup stripped); each rule keeps its own exempt / only key paths. Tested on HEAD 1d5fe5b + the pt-BR copy: 0 hits (L-14, L-9, D-8 clean; build and --pseudo 0 errors; tests 58/58); every rule hits its counter-example in pt-BR-qa.md §5.",
    "keywordMap lists are the complete proposed pt-BR arrays (they replace the current ones). seOwned keeps 'aprender inglês' / 'notícias em inglês' (as broader forms) and adds other English-learning verbs, levelled English news and the chunk word 'blocos' (SurfEnglish's pt-BR site says 'blocos de sentido'; en blocks 'chunks?' the same way). Generic learning words without 'inglês' ('aprender idiomas', 'quem aprende idiomas') stay WordByWord's (R39, R83). reservedG1 is new (pt-BR had none)."
  ],
